{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And they declared their pedigrees after their families.</b> Since their count was in order that they go forth in it as an army for war, the intent was to preserve their lineage, for the merit of their fathers aids them. And the Sages already said (Kiddushin 76a): they do not investigate one who is inscribed in the king's roster (meaning, the soldiers of the house of David). And this is as they said there (ibid.): the Shekhinah rests only upon families of verified lineage in Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:34.557815981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}